WEBVTT

00:00:00.340 --> 00:00:05.780
In the name of the Father and of the Son and of the Holy Spirit, Amen.

00:00:05.780 --> 00:00:13.060
The reading from the Sinaxadion for July 26 on which we commemorate the Holy Virgin

00:00:13.060 --> 00:00:17.610
martyr, Paraskevi of Rome.

00:00:17.610 --> 00:00:26.550
The Holy and Great Marjorie Paraskevi was born during Hadrian's reign in the years 117-138

00:00:26.550 --> 00:00:33.990
in a village near Rome, the daughter of Agathon and Politea, Christian parents, who for many

00:00:33.990 --> 00:00:37.670
years had asked the Lord for a child.

00:00:37.670 --> 00:00:44.750
God, who always fulfills the desires of those who fear Him, gave them a daughter whom they

00:00:44.750 --> 00:00:52.270
named Paraskevi, both because she was born on a Friday and from devotion to the life-giving

00:00:52.270 --> 00:00:56.590
passion of our Lord Jesus Christ.

00:00:56.590 --> 00:01:02.910
From earliest childhood, she consecrated herself entirely to the things of God, feeling

00:01:02.910 --> 00:01:05.950
no attraction for childish games.

00:01:05.950 --> 00:01:12.550
She spent all her time either in church being present at the offices or at home, praying

00:01:12.550 --> 00:01:16.350
or meditating on the Word of God.

00:01:16.350 --> 00:01:22.150
She was 12 years old when her parents died, and she distributed their great wealth to those

00:01:22.150 --> 00:01:29.550
in need, and took the veil, a sign of her consecration to God, after passing some time

00:01:29.550 --> 00:01:35.790
in complete submission to her abyss, being desirous of sharing the treasure of the faith

00:01:35.790 --> 00:01:36.990
with others.

00:01:36.990 --> 00:01:45.270
She left the monastery, and went through towns and villages proclaiming the name of Christ.

00:01:45.270 --> 00:01:51.830
Through her proclamation, she brought many pagans to the true faith, and aroused the hatred

00:01:51.830 --> 00:01:57.630
and jealousy of the Jews, who denounced her to the ruler of the region in which she found

00:01:57.630 --> 00:01:59.150
herself.

00:01:59.150 --> 00:02:06.230
He immediately ordered the arrest of this noble Christian, and had her brought before him.

00:02:06.230 --> 00:02:13.230
When he saw her, he was overcome by her beauty, and quickly tried to win her over through

00:02:13.230 --> 00:02:21.790
flattery, saying, If you let yourself be convinced by my words, and agree to offer sacrifice,

00:02:21.790 --> 00:02:25.750
you will receive great wealth.

00:02:25.750 --> 00:02:33.150
But if you persist in your stubborn refusal, know that I shall hand you over to terrible

00:02:33.150 --> 00:02:36.070
tortures.

00:02:36.070 --> 00:02:41.390
The frail young girl replied to him with a virile boldness.

00:02:41.390 --> 00:02:49.310
I shall never deny my most sweet Jesus Christ, and no torture could ever separate me from

00:02:49.310 --> 00:02:50.990
his love.

00:02:50.990 --> 00:02:59.550
Whatever he said, I am the light of the world, whoever follows me will not walk in darkness,

00:02:59.550 --> 00:03:02.910
but will have the light of life.

00:03:02.910 --> 00:03:09.350
As for your gods, who made neither heaven nor earth, they shall perish from the earth, and

00:03:09.350 --> 00:03:13.440
from under the heavens.

00:03:13.440 --> 00:03:19.680
The king's anger was inflamed, and he gave the order to his soldiers to place a red hot

00:03:19.680 --> 00:03:23.480
helmet on the saint's head.

00:03:23.480 --> 00:03:31.760
Covered in dew, like the three young men in the furnace, Saint Paraskevi felt no suffering.

00:03:31.760 --> 00:03:38.160
Her breasts were cut off, and she was thrown into prison with a heavy stone on top of her

00:03:38.160 --> 00:03:45.400
wounded chest, but was healed by an angel who appeared in a great earthquake.

00:03:45.400 --> 00:03:52.080
Seeing the miracle, 70 of the garrisons' soldiers were converted to Christ.

00:03:52.080 --> 00:03:59.480
At the tyrant's order, they were immediately executed, and Paraskevi was brought before

00:03:59.480 --> 00:04:02.160
him again.

00:04:02.160 --> 00:04:08.680
When she reiterated her ardent confession of faith, the saint was plunged into a bronze

00:04:08.680 --> 00:04:12.600
cauldron, filled with molten lead.

00:04:12.600 --> 00:04:20.640
Yet here too, her body, having received through virginity and askecies, the first fruits of

00:04:20.640 --> 00:04:26.360
future incorruptibility, remained untouched.

00:04:26.360 --> 00:04:32.800
Thinking that the mixture was not at boiling point, the tyrant went up to it, and was blinded

00:04:32.800 --> 00:04:40.000
by the heat of the furnace, recognizing his fault, through the painful consequences he

00:04:40.000 --> 00:04:46.480
began to cry, have pity on me, oh servant of the true God!

00:04:46.480 --> 00:04:53.720
Give me back my sight, and I shall believe in the God whom you proclaim.

00:04:53.720 --> 00:05:01.020
Through the saint's prayers he received not only his sight, but also the light of faith,

00:05:01.020 --> 00:05:10.020
and at his request was baptized in the name of the Holy Trinity, along with all his entourage.

00:05:10.020 --> 00:05:17.100
Once free, saint Paraskevi left the region to continue her mission, finding herself in

00:05:17.100 --> 00:05:21.060
a town governed by a certain esculapios.

00:05:21.060 --> 00:05:26.700
She was proclaiming Christ when she was arrested and brought before the tribunal.

00:05:26.700 --> 00:05:33.940
When esculapios asked her to say who she was, the saint made the sign of the cross, and

00:05:33.940 --> 00:05:40.100
declared that she was a servant of the God who created heaven and earth, who had offered

00:05:40.100 --> 00:05:47.100
himself on the cross for our salvation, and who would return in glory to judge the living

00:05:47.100 --> 00:05:49.100
and the dead.

00:05:49.100 --> 00:05:55.540
The tyrant had her beaten with rods, but the saint continued to glorify God.

00:05:55.540 --> 00:06:05.460
Her gaze turned towards heaven, and when esculapios halted the torturers to ask if she would sacrifice,

00:06:05.460 --> 00:06:10.820
she spat on him with disdain in her eyes.

00:06:10.820 --> 00:06:16.660
Beside himself with rage, he told the soldiers to flay her to the bone.

00:06:16.660 --> 00:06:24.820
Yet after a night spent in the dungeon, the soldiers found her once again unharmed.

00:06:24.820 --> 00:06:31.980
In Paraskevi asked to go to the temple of Apollo, all the pagans rejoiced, thinking she would

00:06:31.980 --> 00:06:36.060
at last agree to offer sacrifice.

00:06:36.060 --> 00:06:43.740
Once there, after long prayer, she made the sign of the cross, and all the idols tumbled

00:06:43.740 --> 00:06:53.100
down, making a great noise, and the people cried out, great is the God of the Christians.

00:06:53.100 --> 00:06:58.860
The priests who were responsible for the idols were outraged, and furiously demanded that

00:06:58.860 --> 00:07:02.180
she be put to death.

00:07:02.180 --> 00:07:09.580
She was thrown into a pit, but by her prayer she put to death the dragon and reptiles that

00:07:09.580 --> 00:07:17.860
were there, realizing that all his attempts had remained totally fruitless, esculapios sent

00:07:17.860 --> 00:07:23.620
the saint to another region, governed by the cruel tarassios.

00:07:23.620 --> 00:07:29.860
While she was healing all the sick who came to her through the invocation of the name of Christ,

00:07:29.860 --> 00:07:36.700
the king summoned her to appear before him, accused her of practicing magic, and had her

00:07:36.700 --> 00:07:43.100
thrown into a stinking pit full of venomous wild beasts.

00:07:43.100 --> 00:07:50.220
Through the sign of the cross, this foul hole became like a fragrant spring meadow, and

00:07:50.220 --> 00:07:57.500
the saint protected by an angel remained untouched by all the other tortures they inflicted

00:07:57.500 --> 00:07:59.940
upon her.

00:07:59.940 --> 00:08:07.380
Unable to contain his rage, the king ordered that the servant of God be beheaded.

00:08:07.380 --> 00:08:13.740
According to her knees, Paraskevi prayed with tears, confiding her courageous soul to

00:08:13.740 --> 00:08:20.380
Christ her spouse, and asking him to grant the forgiveness of sins to all who would honor

00:08:20.380 --> 00:08:22.300
her memory.

00:08:22.300 --> 00:08:29.020
When her head fell under the sword, a heavenly voice was heard, welcoming the saint into

00:08:29.020 --> 00:08:36.020
the kingdom of heaven, a kingdom she had announced by her proclamation and the miracles that

00:08:36.020 --> 00:08:38.420
had accompanied her.

00:08:38.420 --> 00:08:45.940
From that time forth, fragments of her relics scattered in various churches have not ceased

00:08:45.940 --> 00:08:48.820
to accomplish numerous healings.

00:08:48.820 --> 00:08:55.660
In particular, those concerned with diseases of the eye.

00:08:55.660 --> 00:09:01.940
Through the prayers of our Holy Father's O Lord, Jesus Christ our God, have mercy on us

00:09:01.940 --> 00:09:02.940
and save us.
